OpenCode Kiro provider

Compatibility: OpenCode 2.0.23, native @opencode/ai runtime. Not a V1 AI SDK plugin.
Uses direct Kiro inference. OpenCode executes tools and owns permission decisions.

Community plugin: not built by, endorsed by, or affiliated with OpenCode or Kiro.
Repository: https://github.com/vinayshah1998/opencode-provider-kiro

GITHUB INSTALL
Add the version-pinned GitHub plugin to opencode.json / opencode.jsonc:

{
  "plugins": [{
    "package": "github:vinayshah1998/opencode-provider-kiro#v0.1.1",
    "options": { "credentialSource": "cli" }
  }],
  "model": "kiro/auto"
}

Sign in using kiro-cli first. Omit options to use /connect instead. This repository
ships compiled dist files so GitHub installation does not depend on lifecycle
scripts being permitted by the package manager. No npm publication is required.

MANUAL INSTALL
  git clone https://github.com/vinayshah1998/opencode-provider-kiro.git
  cd opencode-provider-kiro

Then follow BUILD and LOCAL INSTALL below.

BUILD
  bun install --frozen-lockfile
  bun run build
  bun test

LOCAL INSTALL
Merge into your OpenCode opencode.json / opencode.jsonc. Use the PACKAGE DIRECTORY,
not dist/plugin.js: OpenCode 2.0.23 rejects configured file paths. Replace the
absolute directory with your checkout path.

{
  "plugins": ["file:///absolute/path/to/opencode-provider-kiro"],
  "model": "kiro/auto"
}

Run /connect, select Kiro, and choose an API key, AWS Builder ID, IAM Identity
Center, existing CLI/IDE session, external IdP session, or Google/GitHub through
kiro-cli. Google/GitHub launches the official CLI login page; select the chosen
provider there. The plugin does not start interactive login on startup.

To explicitly reuse an existing CLI session without importing into OpenCode:

{
  "plugins": [{
    "package": "file:///absolute/path/to/opencode-provider-kiro",
    "options": { "credentialSource": "cli" }
  }],
  "model": "kiro/auto"
}

credentialSource may be "cli" or "ide". reuseCredentials: true checks IDE then
CLI; selecting a specific source avoids mixing accounts. Local credential stores
are read only; rotated OAuth credentials imported through /connect are persisted
by OpenCode. Direct local reuse retains refreshed tokens in memory only.
Use plugin options for startup discovery: OpenCode 2.0.23 applies providers.kiro
settings after plugin setup. Provider-only reuse settings work for inference but
cannot populate discovered models until the first request. Plugin options avoid
this startup ordering issue.

KIRO_API_KEY, KIRO_REGION and KIRO_PROFILE_ARN are supported. Never put tokens,
refresh tokens or client secrets in repository configuration. API keys take
precedence over explicit local reuse. Kiro's own account allowance applies.

The plugin discovers models from the regional profile's management catalog and
adds reasoning variants when supported. Select kiro/<catalog model ID>#<effort>.
Catalog cache is in memory and profile/region-scoped. Discovery retains the
selected connection's inventory until reconnect/restart; failed discovery uses
that profile's last successful in-process catalog or real auto. There is no
persistent cross-session catalog cache.

FEATURES
- AWS binary EventStream framing, CRC validation and bounded incomplete frames.
- Streaming text, separate reasoning/signatures, tool-input fragments and calls.
- User/system/history conversion, multiple tool results, images, and plaintext
  compaction history. OpenCode's native runtime normalizes tool history first.
- CLI/IDE import, device OAuth, social CLI login, token refresh and profile routing.
- Native cancellation/timeouts, quota/rate/context error classification.
- Reported token usage and Kiro credits remain separate. Missing token counts are
  not invented; OpenCode may display zero when Kiro omits them. No USD estimation.

BOUNDARIES
Kiro does not advertise every portable generation control. maxTokens,
temperature and topP produce a warning when unavailable; other unsupported
controls fail explicitly. Forced tools, disabling parallel tools, tool namespaces,
and encrypted cross-provider compaction are rejected rather than silently altered.
Historical reasoning text is not replayed as assistant speech. A reasoning
signature is retained as response metadata, not sent back through an undocumented
request field. Generic transient retry belongs to OpenCode; the provider does not
restart a partially emitted response or execute tools itself.

VERIFICATION
Build and deterministic behavioral tests cover binary framing, tool loops,
cancellation, images, transcript pairing, reasoning configuration, refresh races,
profile-scoped discovery and fresh host credentials. Live OpenCode 2.0.23 smoke:
Kiro auto returned KIRO_PROVIDER_OK; read tool opened a synthetic fixture and Kiro
continued with KIRO_TOOL_ROUNDTRIP_47. Discovered claude-sonnet-4.6#low returned
separate reasoning and text events (323). Sixty regression tests pass.
Interactive new-account login flows are not live-verified. This is a community
integration, not an official Kiro/OpenCode provider; service/API compatibility
can change.
